From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom: wcnss: select non-PD regulators correctly

Pronto v1/v2 have one non-PD regulator and two PD-backed regulators.
Comparing possible PD count with non-PD count skips the offset adjustment
and requests vddcx even when a CX domain is attached. Check the explicit
num_pd_vregs field instead, retaining the Pronto v3 case. SM-T531 logs
show the incorrect dummy vddcx request with a single CX domain.

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_wcnss.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_wcnss.c
@@ -445,19 +445,15 @@
 {
 	const struct wcnss_vreg_info *info = data->vregs;
 	struct regulator_bulk_data *bulk;
-	size_t i, possible_pds = 0, num_vregs = data->num_vregs;
+	size_t i, num_vregs = data->num_vregs;
 	int ret;
-
-	for (i = 0; i < WCNSS_MAX_PDS; i++)
-		if (data->pd_names[i])
-			possible_pds++;
 
 	/*
 	 * If attaching the power domains suceeded we can skip requesting
 	 * the regulators for the power domains. For old device trees we need to
 	 * reserve extra space to manage them through the regulator interface.
 	 */
-	if (possible_pds >= num_vregs) {
+	if (!data->num_pd_vregs) {
 		/* Do nothing if vregs do not include PD regulators (pronto-v3) */
 	} else if (wcnss->num_pds) {
 		info += wcnss->num_pds;
